      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have experienced similar issues, although to varying degrees of severity.  In Geo Locater, for example, while everything was fine on the end of remote players, including the synched data being sent from me to them, on my end anything related to those remote players was broken.  Local logic was fine, however.\n\nPeaking into the logs there were a lot of Udon Behaviors crashing due to \"object not assigned.\"  The visual nature of the bugs lead me to believe that the world correctly recognized how many players were in the instance (OnPlayerJoined fired for everyone and the game spawned an object for each player in the instance) but attempts to get information on these players resulted in null references (the objects spawned for remote players were broken and were labeled with \"Name\" instead of the remote player's name).\n\nFor additional information I joined on them and I would presume neither of those two were on the beta.\n\nI would upload my log but it is slightly over the max (18.9mb).  If you could suggest what data can be safely trimmed from the logs or a way to compress it, I will do so and upload the logs here.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
